      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THYME TO GO (8) returned over 1200m at Gosford last start and was strong late but missed by a neck in an impressive return. Competitive in Saturday company in town last prep so this grade holds no fears. Looks the testing material with added race fitness this evening. SACRED VOW (3) was ridden closer to the speed and did well to hold on for second behind a promising one over 1200m at Kembla last time out. Can improve further with the addition of blinkers for the first time. POSH POMMERY (6) settled at the tail of a small field over 1100m here when fresh from a spell recently and struggled to get involved. Drops 3kgs under this scale and the extra trip is a big help. MENS REA (2) started at $67.0 but exceeded expectations on debut last start, closing well to get up for third behind a subsequent winner over 1100m at Gosford. Looks a serious contender over this more suitable journey. ROCKET GIRL (7) resumes after failing at the only run last prep. McDonald up is a positive sign.",
